66
00:34:04.000 --> 00:34:30.000
A mountain teleported from the wild alien planet of his mind. The one place Niguchi ever felt he really belonged. So it's extremely interesting to me people's place in the world, their sense of belonging, how we function in this planet Earth. I think I have that kind of feeling about sculpture, wanting to be inside the sculpture. It's not just looking at it, it's part of it.

67
00:34:30.000 --> 00:35:22.000
It's your world, it's the world, and the world then becomes a sculpture. Noguchi wanted us to see the world as if we were visiting for the first time, to move our bodies through space as if the simple facts of gravity and contour were brand new delights, to look around with wide eyes, to feel without stretched fingers, and imagine infinite possibilities. In other words, to live like kids on a playground.

